# This holds raw in-progress upload chunks that have not been
# content-validated yet (see ChunkUploadController) - nothing in the app
# ever links to a URL under here, so it's never meant to be reachable.
#
# This previously used Require all denied / Order+Deny to enforce that -
# confirmed live (2026-09-24) that this exact host rejects those
# directives outright (they need Apache's Limit/AuthConfig AllowOverride
# classes, which this host doesn't permit - see Backend/uploads/.htaccess's
# own comment for the 500 that caused there for every uploaded image).
# Switched to RemoveHandler/RemoveType (needs only the FileInfo class,
# confirmed working on this host), same as uploads/.htaccess. This is a
# backup layer, not the primary defense either way: chunk filenames are
# uniqid()-based and scoped under a per-user subdirectory, and nothing in
# this app ever generates a public link into this folder.
RemoveHandler .php .php3 .php4 .php5 .php7 .php8 .phtml .phar .cgi .pl
RemoveType .php .php3 .php4 .php5 .php7 .php8 .phtml .phar .cgi .pl
